<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Vatsa</h1><p class="st-meta">700 BCE – 400 BCE (approx.) · capital Kaushambi</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The kingdom of Kaushambi on the Yamuna, ruled by the romantic hero Udayana and one of the four great powers of the Buddha's age.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Vatsa lay along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yamuna">Yamuna</a> south-west of modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prayagraj">Prayagraj</a>, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kausambi">Kaushambi</a>. Tradition says the Kuru royal house moved there after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hastinapura">Hastinapura</a> was destroyed by a flood, and the Vatsa kings claimed that descent. By the 6th century BCE it was one of the four leading kingdoms, alongside <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-magadha">Magadha</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-kosala">Kosala</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-avanti">Avanti</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kausambi">Kaushambi</a> was a large walled city on the trade routes between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganges-plain">Ganges plain</a> and the west. Its best-known king, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/udayana-of-vatsa">Udayana</a>, a contemporary of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gautama-buddha">Buddha</a>, became the hero of later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a> plays such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhasa">Bhasa's</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/svapnavasavadatta">Svapnavasavadatta</a>, which tells of his love for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vasavadatta">Vasavadatta</a>, daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pradyota">Chanda Pradyota</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-avanti">Avanti</a>. Kaushambi had important Buddhist monasteries, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghositarama">Ghositarama</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/udayana-of-vatsa">Udayana</a> the kingdom declined. It appears to have passed under the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-avanti">Kingdom of Avanti</a> and then, with Avanti, under the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-magadha">Kingdom of Magadha</a> by the 4th century BCE. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kausambi">Kaushambi</a> stayed an important city under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maurya-empire">Mauryas</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shunga-empire">Shungas</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 700 BCE – 400 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">South Asia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:45.77%;width:5.97%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>700 BCE – 400 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kaushambi</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Udayana</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Vedic religion, Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Prakrit</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Vatsa, Vamsa Mahajanapada</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-550&amp;focus=kingdom-of-vatsa" aria-label="Kingdom of Vatsa on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6701 1129 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Vatsa lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7021 1385L7023 15